      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Getting rewarded for the time and effort you put into making VRChat a better place, community leading, making worlds and avatars, getting promoted to Veteran and leading by example. Having the Veteran rank motivated the Trusted Users to be better people, to be good and get ranked up instead of just rotting infront of a mirror, to bring more good to VRC. Then coming back from a week in hospital to find you lot removed Veteran and Legendary ranks. It's disrespectful. You would know that Veteran users in a room were respectable people, that they did good for VRC, now it's just a sea of purple, where even the great Poiyomi is just Trusted User. Where you got a girl who got there by erping and friending hundreds of people or even these days - freaking 10 year old quest kids, next to avatar/world/shader/community creators in terms of reputation and rank. No, I spit on this decision. It wasn't broken, so why fix it. AND not even put it on any update notes. It's disrespected so many people, just more proof that VRC doesn't give a shit about it's clientbase.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
